        "text": "package com.codesnippet.course.lesson04.entity;\n\nimport jakarta.persistence.Entity;\nimport jakarta.persistence.Id;\n@Entity\npublic class Employee {\n    @Id\n    private Integer id;\n    private String name;\n    private String department;\n    private Integer age;\n    public Employee() {}\n    public Employee(Integer id, String name, String department, Integer age) {\n        this.id = id;\n        this.name = name;\n        this.department = department;\n        this.age = age;\n    }\n    public Integer getId() { return id; }\n    public void setId(Integer id) { this.id = id; }\n    public String getName() { return name; }\n    public void setName(String name) { this.name = name; }\n    public String getDepartment() { return department; }\n    public void setDepartment(String department) { this.department = department; }\n    public Integer getAge() { return age; }\n    public void setAge(Integer age) { this.age = age; }\n}\n",
        "explain": [
          "This entity carries the ID and employee details returned by the repository. @Entity describes persistence mapping; it does not itself open a database connection.",
          "The DTO is a separate object. The mapper selects which entity fields are allowed into the client response."
        ]
