      {
        "path": "src/main/java/com/codesnippet/course/lesson13/service/ProductService.java",
        "text": "package com.codesnippet.course.lesson13.service;\n\nimport com.codesnippet.course.lesson13.entity.Product;\nimport com.codesnippet.course.lesson13.repository.ProductRepository;\nimport org.springframework.stereotype.Service;\nimport org.slf4j.Logger;\nimport org.slf4j.LoggerFactory;\n@Service\npublic class ProductService {\n    private static final Logger logger=LoggerFactory.getLogger(ProductService.class);\n    private final ProductRepository repository;\n    public ProductService(ProductRepository repository) { this.repository=repository; }\n    public Product addProduct(Product product) {\n        if(!validateProductName(product.getName())) throw new RuntimeException(\"Product name must not be empty\");\n        logger.info(\"Adding product in DB\"); logger.debug(\"Product name: {}\",product.getName());\n        logger.warn(\"Example warning\"); logger.error(\"Example error-level message\"); logger.trace(\"Example trace\");\n        return repository.save(product);\n    }\n    private boolean validateProductName(String name) { return name!=null && !name.isBlank(); }\n    public Product getProduct(Integer id) { return repository.findById(id).orElseThrow(()->new com.codesnippet.course.lesson13.exception.ProductNotFoundException(\"Product \" + id + \" not found\")); }\n    public Product getByName(String name) { return repository.findByName(name).orElseThrow(()->new com.codesnippet.course.lesson13.exception.ProductNotFoundException(\"Product \" + name + \" not found\")); }\n    public void deleteProduct(Integer id) { repository.deleteById(id); }\n}\n",
        "explain": [
          "The controller calls this service for the product operation. Read any input validation before the repository call: a rejected input should not reach save.",
          "The repository return value is passed back to the caller. In the unit tests, the repository is a mock, so its returned product must be stubbed explicitly."
        ]
      },
      {
        "path": "src/main/java/com/codesnippet/course/lesson13/controller/ProductController.java",
        "text": "package com.codesnippet.course.lesson13.controller;\n\nimport com.codesnippet.course.lesson13.entity.Product;\nimport com.codesnippet.course.lesson13.service.ProductService;\nimport org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.*;\n@RestController\n@RequestMapping(\"/products\")\npublic class ProductController {\n    private final ProductService service;\n    public ProductController(ProductService service) { this.service=service; }\n    @PostMapping public Product add(@RequestBody Product product) { return service.addProduct(product); }\n    @GetMapping(\"/{id}\") public Product get(@PathVariable(\"id\") Integer id) { return service.getProduct(id); }\n    @GetMapping(\"/name/{name}\") public Product byName(@PathVariable(\"name\") String name) { return service.getByName(name); }\n    @DeleteMapping(\"/{id}\") public void delete(@PathVariable(\"id\") Integer id) { service.deleteProduct(id); }\n}\n",
        "explain": [
          "The request path chooses the operation and request binding supplies its arguments. The controller calls ProductService instead of implementing persistence itself.",
          "When the service throws a matching exception, the exception-handler infrastructure constructs the error response instead of returning a product."
        ]
      },
      {
        "path": "src/main/java/com/codesnippet/course/lesson13/exception/ProductNotFoundException.java",
        "text": "package com.codesnippet.course.lesson13.exception;\n\npublic class ProductNotFoundException extends RuntimeException { public ProductNotFoundException(String message) { super(message); } }\n",
        "explain": [
          "Throw this failure when the requested product is absent. Its message travels to the matching handler.",
          "Extending RuntimeException makes it an unchecked failure; the API status comes from the handler, not from this class name."
        ]
      },
      {
        "path": "src/main/java/com/codesnippet/course/lesson13/dto/ErrorResponse.java",
        "text": "package com.codesnippet.course.lesson13.dto;\n\npublic class ErrorResponse {\n    private java.time.LocalDateTime timestamp;\n    private String message;\n    private String details;\n    public ErrorResponse() {}\n    public ErrorResponse(java.time.LocalDateTime timestamp, String message, String details) {\n        this.timestamp = timestamp;\n        this.message = message;\n        this.details = details;\n    }\n    public java.time.LocalDateTime getTimestamp() { return timestamp; }\n    public void setTimestamp(java.time.LocalDateTime timestamp) { this.timestamp = timestamp; }\n    public String getMessage() { return message; }\n    public void setMessage(String message) { this.message = message; }\n    public String getDetails() { return details; }\n    public void setDetails(String details) { this.details = details; }\n}\n",
        "explain": [
          "This object defines the error body sent to the client: timestamp, message, and details.",
          "The accessors matter: a response object needs readable properties to expose its intended fields as JSON."
        ]
      },
      {
        "path": "src/main/java/com/codesnippet/course/lesson13/exception/GlobalExceptionHandler.java",
        "text": "package com.codesnippet.course.lesson13.exception;\n\nimport com.codesnippet.course.lesson13.dto.ErrorResponse;\nimport org.springframework.http.*;\nimport org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.*;\nimport java.time.LocalDateTime;\n@RestControllerAdvice\npublic class GlobalExceptionHandler {\n    @ExceptionHandler(ProductNotFoundException.class)\n    public ResponseEntity<ErrorResponse> handle(ProductNotFoundException exception) {\n        return ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.NOT_FOUND).body(new ErrorResponse(LocalDateTime.now(),exception.getMessage(),\"Product lookup failed\"));\n    }\n}\n",
        "explain": [
          "@RestControllerAdvice makes these exception handlers available across REST controllers. The annotation on each method identifies the exception it handles.",
          "The handler creates a response body and selects its HTTP status. It is not called by an ordinary direct call in ProductController."
        ]
      }
