        "path": "src/main/java/com/codesnippet/course/lesson23/controller/ProductController.java",
        "text": "package com.codesnippet.course.lesson23.controller;\n\nimport com.codesnippet.course.lesson23.entity.Product;\nimport com.codesnippet.course.lesson23.service.ProductService;\nimport org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.*;\n@RestController\n@RequestMapping(\"/products\")\npublic class ProductController {\n    private final ProductService service;\n    public ProductController(ProductService service) { this.service=service; }\n    @PostMapping public Product add(@RequestBody Product product) { return service.addProduct(product); }\n    @GetMapping(\"/{id}\") public Product get(@PathVariable(\"id\") Integer id) { return service.getProduct(id); }\n    @GetMapping(\"/name/{name}\") public Product byName(@PathVariable(\"name\") String name) { return service.getByName(name); }\n    @DeleteMapping(\"/{id}\") public void delete(@PathVariable(\"id\") Integer id) { service.deleteProduct(id); }\n}\n",
        "explain": [
          "The request path chooses the operation and request binding supplies its arguments. The controller calls ProductService instead of implementing persistence itself.",
          "When the service throws a matching exception, the exception-handler infrastructure constructs the error response instead of returning a product."
        ]
