        "path": "src/main/java/com/codesnippet/course/lesson44/Application.java",
        "text": "package com.codesnippet.course.lesson44;\n\nimport org.springframework.boot.SpringApplication;\nimport org.springframework.boot.autoconfigure.SpringBootApplication;\n\n@SpringBootApplication\n@org.springframework.security.config.annotation.method.configuration.EnableMethodSecurity\npublic class Application {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        SpringApplication.run(Application.class, args);\n    }\n\n}\n",
        "explain": [
          "Start here when you run the project. Keep this class in the parent application package so its component scan reaches the packages below it.",
          "SpringApplication.run starts the context and, for a web example, the embedded server. Additional enabling annotations belong to the feature used by this lesson."
        ]
